      {
        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "asr_text": "A 2022 policy brief places today's screen in a longer change. In the U.S., restaurant tipping rose from about 10 to 15 percent in the early 1970s to about 20 percent by the late 1990s. The report argues that digital screens also create guilt tipping. The choice feels less private when a worker is nearby and can see it.",
